{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"A Poet","html":"<article id='sn1.60'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.60 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 1.60 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>6. Jarāvagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>6. Old Age </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kavisutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A Poet </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kiṁsu nidānaṁ gāthānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“What’s the source of verses? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁsu tāsaṁ viyañjanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What constitutes their phrasing? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kiṁsu sannissitā gāthā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What do verses depend upon? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁsu gāthānamāsayo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What underlies verses?” </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Chando nidānaṁ gāthānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Metre is the source of verses. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>akkharā tāsaṁ viyañjanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Syllables constitute their phrasing. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nāmasannissitā gāthā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses depend on names. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kavi gāthānamāsayo”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A poet underlies verses.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Jarāvaggo chaṭṭho. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Jarā ajarasā mittaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vatthu tīṇi janāni ca; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Uppatho ca dutiyo ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kavinā pūrito vaggoti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
